n concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: reliability high, decision quality high, crew atmosphere positive, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Might be a concern for long-distance flights.\n\nCandidate B: stress resilience good, conscientious (reliability), good weather assessment (technical), but uncooperative and grumpy (crew cooperation, communication). Could be problematic.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility serious, concentration, problem solving, adequate response to unexpected events (stress), but arrogant and weak leadership (crew cooperation, communication). Might be okay but leadership weak.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates danger, sees complex connections (technical), leadership good, spatial vision (technical), but unorganized and not good at criticism (adaptability, responsibility). Could be risk.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Which candidate balances strengths and minimal concerns? Candidate C has strong reliability and decision making, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. However \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\" suggests good cooperation despite communication difficulty? Might be contradictory. Egocentric could affect teamwork.\n\nCandidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness, but uncooperative and grumpy - crew cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate D has strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership - crew cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate A has leadership, anticipation, but unorganized and poor at criticism - reliability and adaptability concerns.\n\nProbably Candidate C seems strongest overall: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere positive. Communication difficulty may be mitigated. Also not willing to further education is a concern for adaptability, but maybe less critical than crew cooperation.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the current evidence...\" It's okay.\n\nProvide evidence: 100% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere. Concern: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nExplain why still best: strengths outweigh concerns relative to others.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
